<title>USA: Comcast Corp unit deal upped to $1.7 bln.</title>
<headline>Comcast Corp unit deal upped to $1.7 bln.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Comcast Corp unit Comcast Cable Communications Inc's multi-tranche debt offering was increased to $1.7 billion from an initially planned sale of $1.0 billion, market sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Ba1/BBB-minus rated deal is expected to include the following four tranches, they said.</p>
<p>-$300 million in seven-year notes, upped from $150 million</p>
<p>-$600 million 10-year issue, increased from $400 million,</p>
<p>-$550 million 20-year debt, increased from $200 million,</p>
<p>-$250 million 30-year issue, with a 12-year put option.</p>
<p>The offering is expecte to price later today, sources said.</p>
<p>(( --Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
</text>
